Negative control for ONE scope surface in the chrome (T2.5 · G9 · AC1.1 ·
F5 CORRECTED).

Four loose scope controls in the header is precisely what this task deleted: a
brand popover, an actor menu, a context popover and an impersonation banner, each
its own surface, none of them one cluster. This mutant re-creates that shape with
the smallest possible move — it mounts a second, loose `SessionSwitcher` in the
header beside the bar. The bar is untouched, still grouped, still first, so an
assertion that finds `scope-bar` in the header stays green; only a case that
holds the header to exactly ONE scope surface can see it.

Re-anchored by T3.2, which owns `default.vue` this wave and retired the header's
own Inspector toggle with it. The mutation is unchanged.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the T2.5 layout case asserting the header carries the bar and nothing else
scope-shaped (one `session-switcher` in the chrome, reached through the cluster).

